## Control Signal Rule

Never use `x`, `z`, or don't-care values in generated RTL.

Even when a signal is logically unused for an instruction, assign a deterministic safe value:

```systemverilog
// Safe defaults at top of always_comb
reg_write = 1'b0;
mem_read  = 1'b0;
mem_write = 1'b0;
branch    = 1'b0;
jump      = 1'b0;
alu_srcA  = 1'b0;
alu_srcB  = 2'b00;
wb_sel    = 2'b00;
```

